\code{c(NA, NA)} when regular finite endpoints cannot be obtained.
}

\subsection{\code{parametric_glm_is_regular(fit, term = NULL, tol = 1e-8)}}{

Checks whether a logistic model fit is safe to use for adjusted inference.
\code{fit} is a \code{glm}, \code{term} optionally names a coefficient that must be present,
and \code{tol} controls the boundary thresholds. The helper returns \code{TRUE} only
when the model converged, the design is full rank, fitted probabilities stay
away from \code{0} and \code{1}, the log-likelihood is finite, and any requested term
has finite positive variance. Its role is to reject quasi-separation and rank
deficiency before adjusted \code{LRT} or adjusted \code{SPLRT} proceeds.
}

\subsection{\code{parametric_lm_is_regular(fit, term = NULL, tol = 1e-8)}}{

Performs the corresponding regularity check for the non-atom \code{lm}
fits. The helper returns \code{TRUE} only when the design is full rank, the ML
