}

\subsection{\code{parametric_normal_summary(y0, y1, fits, conf.level, tol = 1e-12)}}{

Summarizes the non-atom Normal component for the unadjusted
parametric procedure. \code{y0} and \code{y1} are the non-atom outcomes in the control
and treatment groups, and \code{fits} is the common model bundle. The helper
returns means, sums of squares, log-likelihood values, the Normal
likelihood ratio statistic, the conditional non-atom mean difference, and its
profile likelihood interval. It explicitly handles zero residual variance and uses an
sums-of-squares fallback when \code{logLik()} is unavailable. Its role is to keep
the Normal component numerically well-defined in exact-fit and near-boundary
settings.
}

